<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiridates I of Armenia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tiridates I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> in the mid-1st century CE and founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsacid-dynasty">Arsacid dynasty</a> of Armenia. A brother of the Parthian king Vologases I, he was placed on the Armenian throne by his brother, provoking war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Under the peace that followed, he travelled to Rome and was crowned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> in 66, so that both empires claimed a stake in Armenia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tiridates-i-of-armenia.jpg" alt="Tiridates I of Armenia" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Panos Terlemezyan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D5%8F%D6%80%D5%A4%D5%A1%D5%BF_%D4%B1_%D5%A9%D5%A1%D5%A3%D5%A1%D5%BE%D5%B8%D6%80._%D5%A8%D5%B6%D5%A4%D6%85%D6%80%D5%AB%D5%B6%D5%A1%D5%AF%D5%B8%D6%82%D5%A9%D5%B5%D5%B8%D6%82%D5%B6_%D6%84%D5%A1%D5%B6%D5%A4%D5%A1%D5%AF%D5%AB%D6%81.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
